<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_tightness" target="ai_infra_market_risk::ai_investment_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Broader, tighter sanctions increase legal/compliance risk and restrict financing and cross‑border partnerships, causing firms and investors to delay or cancel planned AI infrastructure capital deployments.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">ai_infra_market_risk</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_tightness" target="iran_regional_escalation::global_oil_price_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Broader or more intrusive sanctions on Russian energy and finance raise market risk premia and transaction frictions, lifting benchmark oil prices even before or independent of a complete physical supply loss.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">iran_regional_escalation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_tightness" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::investor_confidence_leve" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">Broader and tighter sanctions increase legal and compliance risk for financiers and operators involved with cross-border data-centre deals linked to China, prompting lenders and equity investors to pull back or demand higher risk premia.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_tightness" target="us_domestic_politics::media_attention" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Announcement or escalation of broad, novel sanctions regimes generates immediate news cycles, briefings and opposition scrutiny that increase the volume and prominence of media coverage of the administration and related political debate.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-3 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">us_domestic_politics</data>
</edge>
