<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::energy_export_flow" target="ai_infra_market_risk::compute_capacity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">A sudden reduction in energy export flows raises electricity prices and forces rationing or operational throttling at power‑intensive data centres, reducing active AI compute capacity in affected regions.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">ai_infra_market_risk</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::energy_export_flow" target="iran_regional_escalation::oil_supply_disruption_le" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">Reductions or reroutings of Russian energy shipments (voluntary cuts, export controls or physical interdiction) directly remove traded crude and refined volumes from global distribution, creating immediate physical disruptions in supply chains.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">iran_regional_escalation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::energy_export_flow" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::grid_power_availability" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">A sustained reduction or rerouting of Russian energy exports reallocates limited fuel supplies and raises generation shortages in importing regions, leading to curtailments or higher instability in local grids that lower available power for data centres.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::energy_export_flow" target="us_domestic_politics::candidate_approval" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Sharp reductions or disruptions in global energy exports linked to the war raise US gasoline and heating prices, which directly depress public approval of the incumbent administration and its candidates by worsening pocketbook perceptions.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">us_domestic_politics</data>
</edge>
