<edge source="iran_regional_escalation::military_engagement_inte" target="ai_infra_market_risk::credit_spread" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">Escalation in regional military engagements increases perceived tail and counterparty risk for firms with exposure to the region (including tech suppliers and cloud providers), causing lenders and bond markets to widen corporate credit spreads to price higher default and liquidity risk.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_regional_escalation</data>
  <data key="d40">ai_infra_market_risk</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_regional_escalation::military_engagement_inte" target="ai_infra_market_risk::systemic_interconnectedn" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Sustained military escalation drives governments and large platform/cloud operators to impose stricter regional data/localization rules and to re-architect supply chains and routing, producing deliberate segmentation and reduced coupling across global tech and infrastructure networks.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_regional_escalation</data>
  <data key="d40">ai_infra_market_risk</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_regional_escalation::military_engagement_inte" target="russia_ukraine_war::allied_cohesion" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">A sharp uptick in Iranian-linked kinetic activity draws US/NATO operational attention and forces toward the Middle East and prompts divergent threat-prioritization among partners, reducing political willingness and bandwidth to coordinate or sustain unified support for Ukraine.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_regional_escalation</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_regional_escalation::military_engagement_inte" target="russia_ukraine_war::corporate_market_actions" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Escalating regional conflict increases sanction and insurance risk perceptions, triggering private-sector decisions (asset sales, contract suspensions, insurance withdrawals) to reduce exposure — including accelerated exits or restructurings that alter commercial ties with Russia and regional markets.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_regional_escalation</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_regional_escalation::military_engagement_inte" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::regulatory_scrutiny" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">Escalating regional military activity heightens national‑security concerns and prompts governments to accelerate export controls, investment reviews, and oversight of foreign-linked cloud and data infrastructure, increasing regulatory scrutiny of the sector.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_regional_escalation</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_regional_escalation::military_engagement_inte" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::security_threat_incidenc" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Greater military engagement increases the likelihood of state and proxy kinetic and cyber operations that target communications, undersea cables, ports and hosting facilities, directly raising the incidence and severity of security incidents affecting data‑centres.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_regional_escalation</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_regional_escalation::military_engagement_inte" target="us_domestic_politics::executive_stability" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">A spike in regional kinetic engagements forces the executive into sustained crisis management, producing interagency conflicts, emergency decision cycles, and potential policy reversals that degrade operational steadiness and continuity.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_regional_escalation</data>
  <data key="d40">us_domestic_politics</data>
</edge>
