  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Higher global oil prices produced by Middle East escalation increase domestic energy costs and inflation in sanctioning states, weakening political appetite to expand or tighten sanctions on Russia and leading to more cautious or delayed sanction measures.</data>
