<edge source="us_domestic_politics::media_attention" target="ai_infra_market_risk::systemic_interconnectedn" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Sustained high‑profile media coverage of outages, concentration, or national‑security risks at large cloud/AI providers triggers regulatory reviews and enterprise vendor diversification or data‑localization measures, which reduce cross‑platform and cross‑jurisdiction coupling.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_domestic_politics</data>
  <data key="d40">ai_infra_market_risk</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_domestic_politics::media_attention" target="russia_ukraine_war::tech_control_enforcement" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.55</data>
  <data key="d37">Sharp increases in high-profile media coverage of dual-use technology transfers and breaches generate congressional and public pressure that leads regulators and agencies to issue tighter export-control guidance and enforcement actions.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_domestic_politics</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_domestic_politics::media_attention" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::regulatory_scrutiny" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">A spike in high-profile media coverage of China-related tech risks generates immediate political pressure and public outcry that drives regulators and legislators to open hearings, investigations, and expedited rule-making targeting China-linked tech activities.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_domestic_politics</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
