  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising approval for a candidate known for hawkish China-tech policies increases the perceived probability of restrictive measures (export controls, investment bans), causing investors to pull back or demand higher risk premia for China-exposed tech and data-centre projects.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_domestic_politics</data>
